build: 2026-06-22 v10.41.0 (Real-FFT oscillating spectral rings + non-standard-tuning guard)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notes: NEW since the live v10.40.0: (1) IMMERSIVE VISUAL — the spectral rings now run a REAL FFT of the master output (lock-free tap ring → main-thread EchoelRealFFT, audio-thread-reviewed PASS, no DSP on the audio thread) and render each frequency band as an OSCILLATING WAVEFORM ring (radius wobbles: energy→amplitude, frequency→lobe-count+colour, animated phase, alternating direction). Eased, slow motion (no flashing, WCAG ≤3 Hz; Reduce Motion → frozen FFT shape); silence → black. (2) TUNING GUARD — root-causes the "komische Töne": a persisted non-12-TET tone system silently retunes every generated note (just intonation reads 15–30¢ flat). A clear banner now appears directly under the Create button whenever tuning ≠ 12-TET, naming the active system with a one-tap "12-TET" return to standard; hidden at the default so normal use stays clean. Microtuning stays an intentional feature. Carries everything from v10.40.0 (filter-cutoff automation, key-follow stereo, adaptive brightness, resilient ASC upload retry) and v10.39.0 (komische-Töne sound fixes, Automation, MIDI import, Audio Clips, Unison). All Xcode-Compile-Check green per commit; audio-thread + concurrency reviews on the touched paths.
